title: 'pallet-psm: simplify PSM account handling'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      PSMs no longer manage provider refs on their reserve account and fee destination, so both
      follow the standard account rules.

      - `create_psm` and `remove_psm` no longer touch provider refs.
      - `mint` and `redeem` waive the fee when the fee destination can't receive it.
      - `add_external_asset` requires the reserve account to be able to receive the external
        asset, and fails with `ReserveCannotReceive` otherwise. For a non-sufficient asset, create
        the reserve's asset account first (e.g. with `touch_other`).
      - New `reserve_account` view function returns the reserve account of a PSM instance.

crates:
  - name: pallet-psm
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-assets
    bump: none
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: patch
